  "problem": [
    "(20%) BMI = weight(KG) / height^2(M^2)",
    "For example, 52 Kg, 155 cm, BMI =52 KG/1.55^2 (M^2) = 21.60 ",
    "Input:",
    "(1) height (Integer, cm) ",
    "(2) weight (Integer, pound 磅 ) ",
    "(3) -1 (exit)",
    "(4) 1 M = 100 cm, 1 pound = 0.454 KG",
    "Output:",
    "(1) Normal height: 0.5~2.50 M (0.5<=height<=2.50). Normal weight: 20~300 KG (20<=weight<=300). ",
    "(2) If height not in normal, then output \"Input Height Error\". If weight no in normal, then output \"Input Weight error\". ",
    "(3) If 18.50<=BMI<=24.00,，then output the BMI value(無條件捨去至小數點後第二位). ",
    "(4) If BMI too high (>24.00), then output \"BMI too high\". ",
    "(5) If BMI too low (<18.50), then output \"BMI too low\"."
  ],
